  "question": {
    "text": "A tuning fork arrangement (pair) produces 4 beats / sec with one fork of frequency $288 \\mathrm{cps}$. A little wax is placed on the unknown fork and it then produces 2 beats /sec. The frequency of the unknown fork is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pPVpB",
      "text": "\n286 cps\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jseEJ",
      "text": "\n292 cps\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CGekq",
      "text": "\n294 cps\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WGTSr",
      "text": "\n288 cps",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The fact that placing wax decreases the frequency of the unknown fork and also the beat frequency states that the unknown fork is of higher frequency.\n$$\nn-288=4 \\Rightarrow n=292 \\mathrm{cps}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
